OverTheWire Bandit – Level 0 to Level 1 Report
1. Objective (Level Goal)
The objective of this level is to find the password for bandit1.
The password is stored in a file named readme in the home directory of the bandit0 user.
We need to connect to the Bandit server using SSH, locate the file, read its contents, and use the password to log in to the next level.
2. Tools and Commands Used
Command	Purpose
ssh	Connect to the remote Bandit server
ls	List files and directories
cd	Change the current directory
cat	Display file contents
3. Step-by-Step Procedure
Step 1: Connect to Bandit Level 0
Open the Kali Linux terminal and enter:
ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
Enter the given Bandit Level 0 password when prompted.
Step 2: Check the files
After successful login, type:
ls
This command displays the files in the home directory.
We can see a file named:
readme
Step 3: Read the file
Execute:
cat readme
This displays the contents of the readme file.
The output contains the password required for the next level.
Step 4: Save the password
Copy the displayed password and save it in your personal notes.
Step 5: Log in to Bandit Level 1
Exit the current session:
exit
Connect to the next level:
ssh bandit1@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
Enter the password obtained from the readme file.
If login is successful, you have completed Level 0 to Level 1.
